 "text": "Girl, pause the scroll. Paul is finishing Romans and just casually name-drops her like it's nothing. Phoebe. Sister. Deacon of the church in Cenchreae. Then the line that hits: \"a succourer of many, and of myself also.\" She's the one showing up with cash, cover, connections when the whole operation is about to flop. Paul tells the Roman church straight up: give her whatever she needs, because she has been that for a lot of people including me. She carried the letter that becomes the theological spine of the New Testament. And Paul made sure nobody got to treat her like a side character.",
